# Port Plan — Step 05: The Agent Loop (Ruby → Python)

Port `Boukensha::Agent` — the loop that finally makes the agent *act* — into the
Python step folder, along with the supporting changes that made it possible: a
`parse_response` normalizer on every backend, an `assistant_message` inverse on
three of them, a `tools:` override threaded through `Client` and
`PromptBuilder`, and `max_iterations` / `max_output_tokens` task settings.

This is the sixth of thirteen steps (`00_config` → `12_context`).

> **The delta is much larger than "an `agent.rb` file being added."** `agent.rb`
> is new, but **all five backends** changed, and so did `client.rb`,
> `prompt_builder.rb`, `tasks/base.rb`, `errors.rb`, and `boukensha.rb`. The
> backend changes are not incidental — the loop only stays simple because every
> provider now normalizes its response into one shape. Budget for that.

